167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (This poster presents findings from my internship in the healthcare industry with the SingHealth sustainability team, examining how real-world sustainability work develops professional competencies that extend far beyond classroom learning. Key insights are organised across thematic panels spanning stakeholder coordination, data governance, and behavioural change, to invite dialogue on the tensions between technical and relational dimensions of sustainability practice. As an intern supporting Scope 1 and 2 greenhouse gas emissions reporting, I encountered the operational realities of sustainability management, particularly the challenge of consolidating fragmented data across multiple public health institutions with disparate equipment, data ownership structures, and reporting practices. This experience revealed that sustainability work is fundamentally a coordination exercise, requiring stakeholder engagement, organisational navigation, and professional communication rather than technical expertise alone. Drawing on the concept of Corporate Change Agents for Sustainability \(Schaltegger et al., 2023, 2024\), this poster illustrates how sustainability professionals function as facilitators and coordinators of systemic change. Direct engagement opportunities with local stakeholders during my internship further reinforced the importance of systems thinking and behavioural competencies in addressing interconnected environmental challenges. As I wrap up a co-authored paper from the findings of this internship, these experiences underscore the transferable value of authentic workplace learning for undergraduates in cultivating the adaptive, cross-disciplinary capabilities needed to advance sustainable development goals.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
