179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (Population ageing is reshaping healthcare delivery, long-term care, and sustainable urban wellbeing across East Asian societies, especially in Macao. In Macao, many community-dwelling older adults face multimorbidity and polypharmacy, struggling to interpret medication information, distinguish similar packaging, maintain complex regimens, and communicate health histories during clinical or telehealth consultations. This project introduces Medication Safety Companion, an ageing-friendly AI-enabled platform fostering inclusive, sustainable healthy ageing through responsible innovation. Integrating wearable first-person visual sensing, intelligent text recognition, voice-based interaction, retrieval-augmented knowledge support, and privacy-preserving data management, it assists older adults with medication verification, personalized reminders, pharmaceutical information access, and structured healthcare communication. A human-audited pharmaceutical knowledge framework is incorporated to enhance reliability and minimize risks associated with AI-generated misinformation. By curbing medication mismanagement, the platform also drives sustainable healthcare. Beyond individual safety, this initiative strengthens community resilience by lowering technology and accessibility barriers, supporting intergenerational caregiving, and promoting sustainable practices. The project also embodies student workplace readiness: undergraduates work alongside healthcare professionals, developers, and community organizations, applying classroom knowledge to real-world challenges, cultivating critical thinking and professional skills while contributing to sustainable development and informing policy for age-friendly, environmentally responsible communities.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
